{"id": "138", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded as per section 43(6). This is done under the block concept, where all assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any changes to the block's value must abide by the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961. Additionally, the assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, even if it's not used for the purposes of business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nI need to see the given passages to analyze the physical details and determine the treatment of assets when discarded under the Income Tax Act. Since no passages were provided in your query, I cannot proceed with the reasoning steps or identify specific examples, numbers, or comparisons mentioned in the source material.\nI need the actual passages containing information about the Income Tax Act's treatment of assets when discarded to proceed with the analysis. Without these specific details, I cannot identify the relevant examples, numbers, or comparisons required for the answer. Please provide the passages for analysis.\nI need the actual passages containing information about the Income Tax Act's treatment of assets when discarded to proceed with the analysis. Without these specific details, I cannot identify the relevant examples, numbers, or comparisons required for the answer. Please provide the passages for analysis.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 97.857, "generation_time_seconds": 84.5251, "selection_time_seconds": 13.3314, "nemotron": {"method": "tot", "step_beam_size": 1, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "n_vote": 2, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 2.56, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "139", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded. The block concept is followed, where assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if it is not used for business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nI need to analyze the physical details step by step to determine the next logical reasoning step. Let me examine what I have:\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 69.056, "generation_time_seconds": 58.6784, "selection_time_seconds": 10.3779, "nemotron": {"method": "tot", "step_beam_size": 1, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "n_vote": 2, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 10.53, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "142", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nThe scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded, as per Section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept applies to all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, and any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act. The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even if the asset is not used for business or professional purposes in that year or subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the scrap value from the block in the previous year and claim depreciation on the residual value.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nBased solely on the provided question and the instruction to analyze physical details step by step without adding external information, the next logical reasoning step is to examine the specific physical details mentioned in the question:\nI need to examine the given passages to find information about the treatment of assets when they are discarded under the Income Tax Act. Since no passages have been provided in the current context, I cannot analyze any physical details or extract relevant information.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 90.971, "generation_time_seconds": 78.9845, "selection_time_seconds": 11.9869, "nemotron": {"method": "tot", "step_beam_size": 1, "num_rollout": 4, "num_foresight": 3, "n_vote": 2, "runtime": "transformers-trust-remote-code"}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 5.66, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
