{"id": "189", "question": "how long does it take to make chicken tender in crock pot", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the answer to the question \"How long does it take to make chicken tender in a crock pot?\" is:\n\n6-8 hours on low heat, or 4 hours on high heat if you're short on time.\n\nThe first passage suggests cooking the chicken on low for 6-8 hours, or 1 hour on high and then 5 hours on low. The second passage repeats the same information. The third passage provides additional information that chicken breast will always come out tender as long as there is enough moisture, and suggests cooking it for 4 hours on high if you're short on time.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is 6-8 hours on low heat, or 4 hours on high heat if you're short on time.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_tot", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nAnalyze the text for specific time durations related to cooking chicken in a crock pot, including any temperature settings (e.g., \"low,\" \"high\") and corresponding time ranges (e.g., \"4 hours,\" \"6 hours\"). Check if the passage specifies whether these times apply to chicken specifically or only certain chicken cuts (e.g., breasts vs. thighs). Verify if the duration depends on factors like chicken size, initial temperature, or crock pot model. Ensure all time references are explicitly tied to chicken preparation in a crock pot, not other cooking methods or unrelated details.\nAnalyze the text for specific time durations related to cooking chicken in a crock pot, including any temperature settings (e.g., \"low,\" \"high\") and corresponding time ranges (e.g., \"4 hours,\" \"6 hours\"). Check if the passage specifies whether these times apply to chicken specifically or only certain chicken cuts (e.g., breasts vs. thighs). Verify if the duration depends on f